\'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0UPDATED SET DETAILS (they HAVE changed a little)\
\'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0===================\
\
Although October is the usual month for the annual ARRL SET (Simulated\
Emergency Test), for several years we in the Manhattan area have used\
our participation in the late-September Yellow Brick Road bike Ride\
(YBRR) in place of a more-formal SET.\'a0 Unfortunately this year's YBRR\
was cancelled, so, as the ARES Emergency Coordinator for the Manhattan\
area, I hereby announce an alternate exercise:\
\
Here is the first paragraph of an article from a recent ARRL newsletter:\
\
\'a0 \'a0"Connecticut is a leader in emergency/disaster communications\
\'a0 \'a0 support in all modes for all hazards. The ARRL Section's ARES\
\'a0 \'a0 Region 5 (covering a large portion of the western aspect of the\
\'a0 \'a0 state) executed its third annual simplex test on August 1st.\
\'a0 \'a0 The test, spearheaded by Paul Gibb, KB1TOR, was created to\
\'a0 \'a0 study how communications could be carried out throughout the\
\'a0 \'a0 geographically large Litchfield and northern Fairfield counties\
\'a0 \'a0 without the use of repeaters. The goal of the test is to light\
\'a0 \'a0 up as many EOCs as possible in the region. This year 46 stations\
\'a0 \'a0 participated in the test, which was held on the 2-, 6- and 40-\
\'a0 \'a0 meter bands."\
\
For our 2015 SET, we shall hold an HF SIMPLEX TEST on October 10.\'a0 The\
purpose of this exercise will be to study HF simplex communications\
between our respective stations (including vehicles, if that's where\
your station is) in an attempt to understand when two HF bands are\
dependable and when they are questionable.\'a0 Tests will be made on\
40- and 80-meters.\
\
Technically, I am the ARES EC only for Riley, Geary, and Clay counties,\
but if you live elsewhere (Pottawatomie or Wabaunsee counties or even\
farther afield) and would still like to participate in this exercise,\
PLEASE FEEL FREE to join us; emergencies don't care where you live!-)\
\
I have designed this exercise to interfere in your Saturday life as\
little as possible.\'a0 Here is how it will work:\
\
